=begin
This script is a modified version of #Ruseoffools ;energywings v1.5.4 script.

*Please run ;Compass_and_wings setup first.

This script automates Wing Pin combat abilities based on room context,
NPC status, cooldown availability, target count, enemy spell prep
detection, and optional Leybound Compass abilities. It is designed for
sustained combat situations such as claims or the Dueling Sands while
minimizing redundant commands and respecting ability cooldowns.

The script runs continuously and evaluates combat conditions
approximately twice per second. It also listens for enemy spell prep
messaging in real time and reacts with a wing pin defensive ability.

*Leybound Compass integration:

Optional automatic use of Tier 2 (Temporal Alignment).
- Tier 2 taps the compass before offensive Wing Pin abilities.
Optional automatic use of Tier 3 (Hastened Movements).
- Tier 3 can automatically activate during combat when available.
- Tier 3 includes a configurable minimum hostile target count.
Detects the Compass cooldown message:
[This ability is on cooldown.]

Compass identifying text is configurable to support altered compasses.

  Usage:
    ;Compass_and_Wings
    ;Compass_and_Wings setup

  Features:
  - Only activates while inside your own Lich claim or the Dueling Sands.
  - Automatically detects which wings to use based on the worn wing pin:
      * dark wing-shaped pin  => dark mode
      * pale wing-shaped pin  => light mode
  - Automatically switches mode if you change pins while running.
  - Reacts to enemy spell preparation messaging (KSwole-style):
      * Dark:  pull my wing pin  (Crawling Shadow)
      * Light: pull my wing pin  (Prismatic Aegis)

  Dark wings mode combat abilities:
    - Shadow Mantle: defensive tap ability when not on cooldown.
    - Shadow Barb: single target when prone or stunned.
    - Barbed Sweep: multiple targets (3+) when prone or stunned.
    - Rain of Thorns: AOE when 6+ targets are present.
    - Carrion Guard: defensive AOE when bleeding and 6+ targets are present.

  Light wings mode combat abilities:
    - Luminous Flight: defensive tap ability when not on cooldown.
    - Radiant Pulse: single target when prone or stunned.
    - Blast of Brilliance: multiple targets (3+) when prone or stunned.
    - Blinding Reprisal: AOE when 6+ targets are present.
    - Wings of Warding: defensive AOE when bleeding and 6+ targets are present.


  Mystic Tattoo integration:
  - Configure the exact RUB command in setup (blank disables tattoo use).
  - Compass T3 takes priority; tattoo T5 fills a later combat window.
  - Neither activation is sent while the other ability is active.
  - Mystic Surge is never sent while Mystic Resonance is active.
  - Reads live Effects::Buffs, including effects activated outside this script.
  - Local guards cover effect-update delays. Unknown responses reserve the
    active window and delay retries for three minutes, without claiming success.

  Battle Standard integration:
  - Quiet startup ANALYZE identifies standards, tier, charges and readiness.
  - Supports all permitted altered standard nouns; ambiguous items disable use.
  - Hallowed Reprisal and Ardent Plea have independent setup toggles.
  - Reprisal uses 60/45/30/15 minute cooldowns at tiers 2/3/4/5+.
  - Plea uses a 30 minute cooldown at tier 4, or 15 minutes at tier 5+.
  - Plea waits for a confirmed compass/tattoo haste buff by default.
  - Rally and Final Stand remain manual; passive abilities need no commands.

  Changelog:
    2.2.0 (2026-10-09)
      - Added quiet startup tier/readiness detection and Battle Standard combat abilities.
    2.1.0 (2026-10-06)
      - Added configurable Mystic Tattoo T5 automation and mutual exclusion.
      - Added Mystic Resonance protection and live buff checks after roundtime.
      - Corrected Compass T3's three-minute cooldown and success confirmation.
    2.0.2 (2026-09-03)
      - Removed configurable Leybound Compass naming.
      - Compass detection now looks for an inventory item containing the noun
        "compass", so normal alterations continue to work.
    2.0.1 (2026-08-29)
      - Fixed false/nil-safe message and object matching to prevent NoMethodError
        from calling =~ on false when Lich/game state returns a false value.
      - Hardened Compass command result handling and existing EnergyWings NPC,
        room, pin, command, inventory, and reaction matching.
    2.0.0 (2026-08-29)
      - Leybound Compass integration added without replacing existing EnergyWings settings.
      - Existing per-ability precasts, target thresholds, pause-script settings,
        prep reactions, defensive abilities, Mount Trample behavior, and all
        prior EnergyWings configuration keys are preserved.
  
  Author: Khaell, Ruseoffools, Codex
  Tags: combat, automation, wing pin, lich, cooldowns, aoe, claim, dueling sands, energywings, leybound compass, mystic tatoo, battle standard
  Version: 2.2.0
=end

# UTF-8 safe. Uses only ASCII characters in strings and comments.

require 'thread'

module EnergyWings
module_function

VERSION = '1.6.11'
ABILITY_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 2
MOUNT_TRAMPLE_TRIGGER_WINDOW_SECONDS = 8
DEFAULT_SCRIPTS_TO_PAUSE = %w[bigshot hunt3].freeze unless defined?(DEFAULT_SCRIPTS_TO_PAUSE)
DEFAULT_PRECAST_FOR_ABILITY = {
  'Shadow Barb' => 'incant 118',
  'Barbed Sweep' => 'incant 110',
  'Rain of Thorns' => "invoke 1714 tat\ncast",
  'Carrion Guard' => '',
  'Shadow Mantle' => '',
  'Crawling Shadow' => '',
  'Luminous Flight' => '',
  'Radiant Pulse' => '',
  'Blast of Brilliance' => '',
  'Blinding Reprisal' => '',
  'Wings of Warding' => '',
  'Prismatic Aegis' => ''
}.freeze unless defined?(DEFAULT_PRECAST_FOR_ABILITY)
DEFAULT_SETTINGS = {
  use_prep_reaction: true,
  use_defensive_tap: true,
  use_single_target: true,
  use_multi_target: true,
  use_aoe: true,
  use_aoe_after_mount_trample: false,
  use_guard_aoe: true,
  multi_target_threshold: 3,
  aoe_target_threshold: 4,
  guard_target_threshold: 4,
  pause_bigshot: DEFAULT_SCRIPTS_TO_PAUSE.include?('bigshot'),
  additional_pause_scripts: 'hunt3',
  use_leybound_compass: true,
  use_compass_t2: true,
  use_compass_t3: true,
  compass_t3_min_targets: 1,
  use_mystic_tattoo: true,
  mystic_tattoo_command: '',
  mystic_tattoo_min_targets: 1,
  use_battle_standard: true,
  use_hallowed_reprisal: true,
  use_ardent_plea: true,
  ardent_plea_with_haste: true,
  battle_standard_min_targets: 1
}.freeze unless defined?(DEFAULT_SETTINGS)
PAUSE_OWNER_KEY = 'energywings'

# ----------------------------
# Helpers
# ----------------------------

def setup_mode?
  Script.current.vars[1].to_s =~ /\Asetup\z/i
end


def scripts_to_pause
  scripts = []
  scripts << 'bigshot' if @settings[:pause_bigshot]
  scripts.concat(parse_script_list_setting(@settings[:additional_pause_scripts]))
  scripts.map(&:strip).reject(&:empty?).uniq
end

def in_allowed_room?
  Lich::Claim.mine? || Room.current.location.to_s =~ /Dueling Sands/
end

def living_npc
  GameObj.targets.find { |n| n && n.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

def find_wing_pin
  # Your inventory showed: "dark wing-shaped pin" (no "a/an")
  GameObj.inv.find { |i| i && i.name.to_s =~ /\A(?:dark|pale)\s+wing-shaped\s+pin\z/i }
end

def wing_pin_mode(pin)
  return nil unless pin
  return "dark"  if pin.name.to_s =~ /\Adark\s+wing-shaped\s+pin\z/i
  return "light" if pin.name.to_s =~ /\Apale\s+wing-shaped\s+pin\z/i
  nil
end

def ability_ready?(name)
  !Effects::Cooldowns.active?(name)
end

def cooldown_active_name?(name)
  return true if Effects::Cooldowns.active?(name)

  needle = name.to_s.downcase
  (Effects::Cooldowns.to_h || {}).keys.any? { |key| key.to_s.downcase.include?(needle) }
rescue StandardError
  false
end

def update_mount_trample_trigger_state
  active_now = cooldown_active_name?('Mount Trample')
  @mount_trample_cooldown_active = false if @mount_trample_cooldown_active.nil?

  if active_now && !@mount_trample_cooldown_active
    @pending_mount_trample_aoe_until = Time.now + MOUNT_TRAMPLE_TRIGGER_WINDOW_SECONDS
  end

  @mount_trample_cooldown_active = active_now

  if @pending_mount_trample_aoe_until && Time.now > @pending_mount_trample_aoe_until
    @pending_mount_trample_aoe_until = nil
  end
rescue StandardError
  nil
end

def mount_trample_aoe_triggered?
  update_mount_trample_trigger_state
  @pending_mount_trample_aoe_until && Time.now <= @pending_mount_trample_aoe_until
end

def consume_mount_trample_aoe_trigger
  @pending_mount_trample_aoe_until = nil
end


# ----------------------------
# Leybound Compass integration
# ----------------------------

def find_leybound_compass
  # Leybound Compasses always retain the noun "compass".
  # Alterations may change the adjective, but not the noun.
  GameObj.inv.find do |obj|
    obj && obj.name.to_s =~ /\bcompass\b/i
  end
end

# The compass can be altered, so match only the invariant GSIV messaging.
def compass_t2_success_message?(message)
  text = message.to_s
  text =~ /needle begins to spin through a blur of possible moments/i ||
    text =~ /future converges upon a single point/i
end

def compass_ability_on_cooldown?(message)
  message.to_s =~ /\[This ability is on cooldown\.\]/i
end

def activate_compass_t2_command
  compass = find_leybound_compass
  return :missing unless compass

  result = nil
  with_paused_scripts do
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    # Wait specifically for either the Temporal Alignment success text or the
    # shared Leybound Compass cooldown message.  This avoids depending on the
    # altered material/name of the compass.
    result = dothistimeout("tap ##{compass.id}", 4, /needle begins to spin through a blur of possible moments|future converges upon a single point|\[This ability is on cooldown\.\]/i)
  end

  text = result.to_s
  return :success if compass_t2_success_message?(text)
  return :cooldown if compass_ability_on_cooldown?(text)
  :failed
rescue StandardError
  :failed
end

def compass_t2_ready?
  return false unless @settings[:use_leybound_compass] && @settings[:use_compass_t2]
  return false unless find_leybound_compass
  return false if @compass_t2_cooldown_until && Time.now < @compass_t2_cooldown_until
  return false if @compass_t2_attempted_at && (Time.now - @compass_t2_attempted_at) < 2

  # Use Lich cooldown data when available, while retaining the local timer as
  # a fallback because the Compass effect is not guaranteed to appear there.
  !['Temporal Alignment', 'Leybound Compass T2'].any? { |n| cooldown_active_name?(n) }
end

# Buffs and cooldowns are separate: Resonance's cooldown must not block Surge
# after its actual ten-second buff has ended. Fail closed if live state cannot
# be read, rather than risk wasting a conflicting activation.
def live_buff_active?(name)
  return true if Effects::Buffs.active?(name)
  needle = name.downcase
  Effects::Buffs.to_h.keys.any? { |key| key.to_s.downcase.include?(needle) }
rescue StandardError
  true
end

def haste_cooldown_active?(names)
  names.any? do |name|
    Effects::Cooldowns.active?(name) ||
      Effects::Cooldowns.to_h.keys.any? { |key| key.to_s.downcase.include?(name.downcase) }
  end
rescue StandardError
  true
end

def combat_haste_active?
  (@combat_haste_reserved_until && Time.now < @combat_haste_reserved_until) ||
    live_buff_active?('Hastened Movements') || live_buff_active?('Mystic Surge')
end

def compass_t3_ready?
  return false unless @settings[:use_leybound_compass] && @settings[:use_compass_t3]
  return false unless find_leybound_compass
  return false if combat_haste_active?
  return false if @compass_t3_cooldown_until && Time.now < @compass_t3_cooldown_until
  !haste_cooldown_active?(['Hastened Movements', 'Leybound Compass T3'])
end

def mystic_tattoo_ready?
  return false unless @settings[:use_mystic_tattoo]
  return false if @settings[:mystic_tattoo_command].to_s.empty?
  return false if combat_haste_active? || live_buff_active?('Mystic Resonance')
  return false if @mystic_tattoo_cooldown_until && Time.now < @mystic_tattoo_cooldown_until
  !haste_cooldown_active?(['Mystic Surge'])
end

# Serialize both activations and check live state AFTER waiting out RT/cast RT.
# No success-message guesses: only a live buff confirms activation. Reserve
# 30 seconds plus a two-second delivery margin even if confirmation is delayed.
def activate_combat_haste(kind, target_count)
  threshold = kind == :compass ? :compass_t3_min_targets : :mystic_tattoo_min_targets
  return false if target_count < @settings[threshold]

  (@combat_haste_mutex ||= Mutex.new).synchronize do
    with_paused_scripts do
      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      return false unless in_allowed_room? && living_npc && !hidden? && !checkstunned
      return false if GameObj.targets.count < @settings[threshold]
      ready = kind == :compass ? compass_t3_ready? : mystic_tattoo_ready?
      return false unless ready

      if kind == :compass
        compass = find_leybound_compass
        return false unless compass
        command = "rub ##{compass.id}"
        effect = 'Hastened Movements'
        @compass_t3_cooldown_until = Time.now + 180
      else
        command = @settings[:mystic_tattoo_command]
        effect = 'Mystic Surge'
        @mystic_tattoo_cooldown_until = Time.now + 180
      end
      @combat_haste_reserved_until = Time.now + 32
      # PUT sends once without consuming listener lines or retrying RUB.
      put command
      deadline = Time.now + 3
      confirmed = false
      loop do
        # Do not use the fail-closed guard as a success confirmation.
        confirmed = Effects::Buffs.active?(effect) rescue false
        break if confirmed || Time.now >= deadline
        sleep 0.1
      end
      if confirmed
        @combat_haste_reserved_until = Time.now + 32
        echo "#{effect.upcase} {!}".center(55)
      else
        echo "#{effect}: activation sent but unconfirmed; overlap guard and 3-minute retry delay retained."
      end
      confirmed
    end
  end
rescue StandardError => e
  echo "combat haste error: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
  false
end

def activate_compass_t2
  return false unless compass_t2_ready?
  @compass_t2_attempted_at = Time.now

  case activate_compass_t2_command
  when :success
    # Tier 2 has a three-minute cooldown.  Start the local guard only after
    # the actual GSIV success message confirms Temporal Alignment fired.
    @compass_t2_cooldown_until = Time.now + 180
    echo 'LEYBOUND COMPASS T2: TEMPORAL ALIGNMENT {!}'.center(55)
    true
  when :cooldown
    # We received the exact shared Compass cooldown response.  Prevent spam
    # for the known three-minute cooldown window.
    @compass_t2_cooldown_until = Time.now + 180
    false
  else
    false
  end
end

def activate_compass_t3(target_count)
  return false unless compass_t3_ready?
  activate_combat_haste(:compass, target_count)
end

def activate_mystic_tattoo(target_count)
  return false unless mystic_tattoo_ready?
  activate_combat_haste(:tattoo, target_count)
end

def prepare_compass_for_attack
  activate_compass_t2
end


# ----------------------------
# Battle Standard integration
# ----------------------------

BATTLE_STANDARD_NOUNS = %w[standard flag banner ensign pennant pennon banderole banderol bannerol oriflamme gonfalon].freeze
STANDARD_ANALYZE_TIMEOUT = 5

def battle_standard_candidates
  GameObj.inv.select do |obj|
    obj && BATTLE_STANDARD_NOUNS.include?(obj.name.to_s.downcase.split.last)
  end
end

def parse_battle_standard_analyze(text)
  match = text.match(/\bThis is a tier\s+(\d+)\s+Battle Standard\./i)
  return nil unless match && (1..6).include?(match[1].to_i)
  states = {}
  text.scan(/^\s*(Hallowed Reprisal|Ardent Plea|Final Stand|Rally)\s*\[[^\]]+\]:\s*(Ready|On Cooldown)\s*$/i) do |name, status|
    states[name.downcase] = status.downcase == 'ready'
  end
  charges = text.match(/^\s*Charges:\s*(\d+)\s*$/i)
  { tier: match[1].to_i, charges: charges && charges[1].to_i, ready: states }
end

def standard_cooldown_seconds(tier, ability)
  return nil unless (1..6).include?(tier.to_i)
  case ability
  when 'Hallowed Reprisal'
    tier >= 2 ? (60 - 15 * [tier - 2, 3].min) * 60 : nil
  when 'Ardent Plea'
    tier >= 4 ? (tier >= 5 ? 15 : 30) * 60 : nil
  end
end

# Suppress only recognized analyze lines, preserving XML tags and unrelated
# combat output. Never globally squelch the game or swallow the prompt.
def standard_analyze_line?(text)
  text.strip.empty? || text =~ /\A\s*(?:You analyze .+ and sense that the creator has provided the following information:|This is a tier \d+ Battle Standard\.|Tier|[1-6]: (?:Rally|Hallowed Reprisal|Reckoning|Ardent Plea|Divine Bulwark|Final Stand)\b.*|(?:Attunement|Charges|Deity|Deity Primary Color|Deity Secondary Color):.*|(?:Rally|Hallowed Reprisal|Ardent Plea|Final Stand)\s*\[[^\]]+\]:.*|If the standard's deity conversion ability.*|The battle standard can be TUCKed.*|This is a flag on a pole.*|There will always be a reference to the pole.*|The battle standard may not be lightened\.)\s*\z/i
end

def quiet_standard_analyze(obj)
  return nil unless defined?(DownstreamHook)
  hook_name = "energywings_standard_analyze_#{object_id}"
  lines = []
  collecting = false
  finished = false
  hook_added = false
  with_paused_scripts do
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    analyze_hook = proc do |raw|
      # Hooks receive raw XML. Strip tags only for recognition/parsing, retaining
      # them in the returned stream so the client's protocol remains intact.
      output = raw.to_s.lines.map do |line|
        plain = line.gsub(/<[^>]*>/, '').strip
        collecting = true if plain =~ /\AYou analyze .+ and sense that the creator has provided the following information:/i
        if collecting
          lines << plain
          finished = true if plain =~ /\AThe battle standard may not be lightened\./i || line.include?('<prompt')
          if standard_analyze_line?(plain) && !line.include?('<prompt')
            line = line.gsub(/(^|>)[^<]+/) { |part| part.start_with?('>') ? '>' : '' }
          end
        end
        line
      end.join
      output.empty? ? nil : output
    end
    # Newer Lich releases can also remove this hook automatically on script
    # death. Older releases still use the ensure cleanup below.
    if DownstreamHook.method(:add).parameters.any? { |_kind, name| name == :persist }
      DownstreamHook.add(hook_name, analyze_hook, persist: false)
    else
      DownstreamHook.add(hook_name, analyze_hook)
    end
    hook_added = true
    put "analyze ##{obj.id}"
    deadline = Time.now + STANDARD_ANALYZE_TIMEOUT
    sleep 0.05 until finished || Time.now >= deadline
    # Require the entire response, not just the tier line. Partial analysis
    # lacks readiness data and is unsafe to use after a script restart.
    return nil unless finished
    parse_battle_standard_analyze(lines.join("\n"))
  end
rescue StandardError => e
  echo "Battle Standard analysis unavailable: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
  nil
ensure
  DownstreamHook.remove(hook_name) if hook_added
end

def initialize_battle_standard
  @battle_standard = nil
  @standard_cooldown_until = {}
  @standard_active_until = {}
  return unless @settings[:use_battle_standard]
  detected = battle_standard_candidates.map do |obj|
    data = quiet_standard_analyze(obj)
    data && data.merge(id: obj.id, name: obj.name)
  end.compact
  if detected.size != 1
    echo "Battle Standard automation disabled: #{detected.empty? ? 'no standard could be identified' : 'multiple standards found; carry only the standard you want automated'}."
    return
  end
  @battle_standard = detected.first
  if @battle_standard[:charges] == 0
    echo 'Battle Standard automation disabled: the standard has no charges.'
    @battle_standard = nil
    return
  end
  ['Hallowed Reprisal', 'Ardent Plea'].each do |ability|
    cooldown = standard_cooldown_seconds(@battle_standard[:tier], ability)
    # Missing status is also treated conservatively as unavailable.
    if cooldown && @battle_standard[:ready][ability.downcase] != true
      @standard_cooldown_until[ability] = Time.now + cooldown
    end
  end
  reprisal = standard_cooldown_seconds(@battle_standard[:tier], 'Hallowed Reprisal')
  plea = standard_cooldown_seconds(@battle_standard[:tier], 'Ardent Plea')
  echo "Battle Standard T#{@battle_standard[:tier]} detected: Reprisal #{reprisal ? "#{reprisal / 60}m" : 'locked'}, Plea #{plea ? "#{plea / 60}m" : 'locked'} cooldowns."
end

def standard_haste_confirmed?
  # Unknown state must never be taken as confirmation of an active haste buff.
  Effects::Buffs.active?('Hastened Movements') || Effects::Buffs.active?('Mystic Surge')
rescue StandardError
  false
end

def battle_standard_ready?(ability)
  return false unless @settings[:use_battle_standard] && @battle_standard
  return false unless GameObj.inv.any? { |obj| obj && obj.id == @battle_standard[:id] }
  return false unless standard_cooldown_seconds(@battle_standard[:tier], ability)
  toggle = ability == 'Hallowed Reprisal' ? :use_hallowed_reprisal : :use_ardent_plea
  return false unless @settings[toggle]
  return false if @standard_cooldown_until[ability] && Time.now < @standard_cooldown_until[ability]
  return false if @standard_active_until[ability] && Time.now < @standard_active_until[ability]
  return false if live_buff_active?(ability) || haste_cooldown_active?([ability])
  return false if ability == 'Ardent Plea' && @settings[:ardent_plea_with_haste] && !standard_haste_confirmed?
  true
end

def activate_battle_standard(ability)
  return false unless battle_standard_ready?(ability)
  with_paused_scripts do
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    return false unless in_allowed_room? && living_npc && !hidden? && !checkstunned
    return false if GameObj.targets.count < @settings[:battle_standard_min_targets]
    return false unless battle_standard_ready?(ability)
    verb = ability == 'Hallowed Reprisal' ? 'clench' : 'raise'
    success = ability == 'Hallowed Reprisal' ? /As you reach for your battle standard and clench it in your fist/i : /As you raise your battle standard high/i
    duration = ability == 'Hallowed Reprisal' ? 180 : 30
    # Reserve first: an unrecognized response cannot cause repeated attempts.
    @standard_cooldown_until[ability] = Time.now + standard_cooldown_seconds(@battle_standard[:tier], ability)
    @standard_active_until[ability] = Time.now + duration + 2
    result = dothistimeout("#{verb} ##{@battle_standard[:id]}", 4, Regexp.union(success, /cooldown|must wait|not ready|no charges|not attuned/i))
    if result.to_s =~ success
      echo "#{ability.upcase} {!}".center(55)
      true
    else
      echo "#{ability}: activation unconfirmed; tier-based retry delay retained."
      false
    end
  end
rescue StandardError => e
  echo "Battle Standard activation error: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
  false
end

# ----------------------------
# Spell prep detection (from KSwole)
# Paste/expand as needed. This is the key wiring point.
# ----------------------------

CREATURE_SPELL_PREPS_WING_PIN = Regexp.union(
    # Atoll and Nelemar
    /^An? (?:.*)\belemental utters an incantation in an unfamiliar, bubbling language\./,
    /^An? (?:.*)\b(?:fanatic|radical) steeples (?:his|her) clawed fingers together, murmuring a quick incantation\./,
    /^An? (?:.*)\bsiren begins singing a sweet song\./,
    /^An? (?:.*)\b(?:magus|warden) makes a subtle gesture, drawing traces of faint blue-green light into (?:his|her) webbed hands\./,
    /^An? (?:.*)\b(?:warlock|dissembler|sentry|psionicist) chants in an incomprehensible language, causing streams of dim grey energy to lash about (?:his|her) (?:hands|golden claws)\./,

    # Bonespear
    /^(?:.*) draws an ancient sigil in the air\./,

    # Bowels
    /^An? (?:.*)\belder invokes the power of (?:his|her) god, the symbol on (?:his|her) forehead glowing brightly\./,
    /^An? (?:.*)\bjarl traces a simple symbol as (?:he|she) reverently calls upon the power of (?:his|her) god\./,

    # Citadel
    /^An? (?:.*)\bapprentice whispers a magical incantation, bending the elements to (?:his|her) whim\./,
    /^An? (?:.*)\bherald seethes a forceful chant, commanding the spirits to do (?:his|her) bidding\./,

    # Confluence
    /^(?:.*) glows with a bright blue light\./,
    /^(?:.*) rumbles with an inner power\./,
    /^(?:.*) utters an incantation in an unfamiliar, bubbling language\./,
    /^(?:.*) whispers an incantation into the wind\./,
    /^(?:.*) raises a molten appendage/,
    /^(?:.*) sparks wildly/,
